      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add multi-class artifact viewer",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- add an in-app, read-only artifact viewer for code, text, Markdown, PDF, DOCX, and uploaded HTML files\r\n- replace document download-only cards with an accessible open action while preserving downloads and existing image/audio/video behavior\r\n- add desktop side-pane and mobile full-screen presentation with focus restoration, Escape handling, loading states, and pane-local fallbacks\r\n- classify using stored upload MIME metadata plus the original filename because unsafe upload types are served as `application/octet-stream`\r\n- add the viewer dependencies, embedded production assets, documentation, and browser coverage\r\n\r\n## Viewer behavior\r\n\r\n- code and text render as inert escaped source with `highlight.js` for known languages\r\n- Markdown supports sanitized preview and source modes through the existing `marked` and DOMPurify pipeline\r\n- PDF supports one-page-at-a-time navigation, page counts, and zoom using the existing `pdfjs-dist` integration\r\n- DOCX converts semantically in-browser with Mammoth and sanitizes the resulting HTML\r\n- uploaded HTML is sanitized, placed in an empty-sandbox `iframe.srcdoc`, and constrained by a CSP that permits only inline styles and local `data:`/`blob:` assets\r\n- unsupported files show metadata and a download fallback without execution\r\n\r\n## Safety contract\r\n\r\n- text, code, Markdown, and HTML previews are limited to 2 MiB\r\n- DOCX conversion is limited to 16 MiB; PDF preview uses the existing 64 MiB upload ceiling\r\n- previews use same-origin authenticated fetches, abort on close/switch, and release PDF resources\r\n- HTML scripts, forms, frames, external links/resources, and network-bearing CSS references are removed before rendering; server download headers and CSP are unchanged\r\n- v1 is read-only and does not add artifact storage, editing, collaboration, or CRDT state\r\n- no database, OpenAPI, SDK, or public transport contract changes\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- `pnpm check`\r\n- `pnpm coverage` — 86.5% total Go coverage\r\n- `pnpm test:e2e` — 48 passed\r\n- `pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/artifact-viewer.spec.ts` — 4 passed, covering classification, highlighting, Markdown source/preview, PDF page/zoom, DOCX, HTML isolation, oversized/malformed fallbacks, mobile sizing, and `message.updated`\r\n- production web/SDK build and embedded asset refresh completed through the E2E web server\r\n- browser visual inspection completed for the desktop side pane and mobile full-screen layout\r\n\r\n## Real behavior proof\r\n\r\nThese captures come from the local OpenClaw → ClickClack delivery path and the running viewer using Markdown file as the test point:\r\n\r\n### Behavior while testing PR\r\n![Markdown preview side pane](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jjjhenriksen/clickclack/3d94e34/docs/proof/artifact-viewer-markdown-preview.png)\r\n\r\n![Markdown source side pane](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jjjhenriksen/clickclack/3d94e34/docs/proof/artifact-viewer-markdown-source.png)\r\n\r\n### Current behavior before merging PR\r\n![OpenClaw-delivered ClickClack attachment](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jjjhenriksen/clickclack/3d94e34/docs/proof/openclaw-clickclack-attachment.png)\r\n\r\n![Download control behavior](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jjjhenriksen/clickclack/3d94e34/docs/proof/openclaw-download-permission.png)\r\n\r\n## Out of scope\r\n\r\n- OpenClaw `sendMedia` delivery remains a separate companion PR\r\n- collaborative Markdown, mutable uploads, revisioned artifacts, and Jot/CRDT storage remain follow-up work",
        "branch": "codex/artifact-viewer",
